WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.168 --> 00:00:03.680 line:15%
(upbeat accordion music)

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.250 line:15%
The purpose of my trip was to highlight

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.240
the positive attributes of Haiti and its people,

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.200
but it's impossible to ignore Haiti's ongoing crises.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.380
As the poorest country in the western hemisphere,

6
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.040
over 50% of Haitians live on less than two dollars a day

7
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.450
and the country is plagued by a stagnant economy,

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.670
government corruption and a lack of healthcare,

9
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.750
clean water and education.

10
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.890
Add to that the many misconceptions about Haiti

11
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.460
that are perpetuated by the media.

12
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.780
Take crime, for example.

13
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.740
Haiti actually has one of the lowest violent crime rates

14
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.820
of any island in the Caribbean.

15
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.550
Yet in spite of all these challenges,

16
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.340
resilient Haitians are determined to lead their country

17
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.840
into a better future.

18
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.880
I met with a collective

19
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.870
of extraordinary expat business women

20
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.800
who have decided to return to their homeland

21
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.730
to kickstart the economic recovery of Haiti.

22
00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.310
I'm standing here with Paula and Margaret

23
00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:52.510
and they're part of something

24
00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.800 line:15%
that's really incredible here in Haiti, you call it DOT.

25
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.870 line:15%
This is an initiative, a collective.

26
00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.930 line:15%
It's all women.

27
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.763 line:15%
Yes.

28
00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:05.763
And women are a huge part of the economic resurgence

29
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.934
for Haiti, isn't that right?

30
00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:07.970
Absolutely.

31
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.000
Haitians like to say that women carry the country.

32
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.410
Yeah, I have a 14-year-old daughter

33
00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.142
and every day she tells me women are the future

34
00:01:15.142 --> 00:01:17.220
and I think actually the future is now.

35
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.110
Hi, what's your name?

36
00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:18.943
[Regine] Regine.

37
00:01:18.943 --> 00:01:20.107
Hi, Regine, how are you, where are you from?

38
00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:21.740
I'm originally, well, from Haiti,

39
00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.430 line:15%
but I was born and raised in Boston.

40
00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.340 line:15%
I moved back to Haiti when I was 25.

41
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.480
And what is it that you're making here?

42
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.870
Please tell me alcohol's involved.

43
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.290
Alcohol is definitely involved.

44
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.480
We produce cocktails, hot sauces,

45
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.440
iced teas and cooking sauces.

46
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.210
Okay, I'm gonna zero right in on the cocktail.

47
00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.250
On the cocktail.

48
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.060
Just because time is of the essence.

49
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.230
So this is a (speaking Haitian Creole).

50
00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.360
Haitian blackberries with the grapefruit.

51
00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.363
Okay, a little more.

52
00:01:47.363 --> 00:01:49.446
A little more, all right.

53
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.372
There's still a little room at the top.

54
00:01:53.372 --> 00:01:55.340
Thank you, now we're talking, okay.

55
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:57.833
Here we go.

56
00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.040
That is really good.

57
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.080
I don't wanna stop drinking this.

58
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:03.913
I can give you more.

59
00:02:03.913 --> 00:02:04.746
You can have that

60
00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:05.579
or you can try the other ones.
Now you know what

61
00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:06.412
you're doing?

